<title>RUSSIA: Russian 301-day T-bill yields 34.70 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 301-day T-bill yields 34.70 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of 301-day GKO discount Treasury bills was 34.70 percent on Wednesday, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the yield would be in the 32.3-35.5 percent range.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>    Series number		    22077</p>
<p>    Issue volume		     7.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)		   8.09 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)		   6.21 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds			   4.83 trln</p>
<p>    Average price		    77.75 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price	  77.44 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield		    34.70  pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield	 35.33 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor				301 day</p>
<p>    Maturity date		    Jan 14, 1998</p>
<p>On March 19 the Finance Ministry will offer four trillion roubles in 175-day T-bills (series 22076) and repay about 6.63 trillion roubles in maturing six-month T-bills (series 22045).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
